\npadding: 16px !important;\r\n}\r\n.hq-cta img{\r\nwidth:64px !important;\r\n}\r\n.hq-cta-text-header{\r\ndisplay:block;\r\nfont-size: 14px !important;\r\nline-height:17.5px !important;\r\n-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.hq-cta-text-body{\r\ndisplay:block;\r\nmargin-top:8px !important;\r\nline-height:13.75px !important;\r\nfont-size: 11px !important;\r\n-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\r\n}\r\n}\r\n</style><link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=PT+Mono&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\"><!--[if mso]><style type=\"text/css\">\r\n.b, .s  {font-family: Arial, Helvetica, Helvetica, sans-serif !important;}\r\n.v {font-family: Georgia, Palatino Linotype, serif !important;}\r\n.ol-adpad {padding-bottom: 10px !important;}\r\na {color: #222222; text-decoration:underline !important;}\r\n</style><![endif]--><!--[if gte mso 7]><xml><o:OfficeDocumentSettings><o:AllowPNG/><o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch></o:OfficeDocumentSettings></xml><![endif]--></head><body style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0; text-align: center;\"><div style=\"display:none;font-size:1px;color:#222222;line-height:1px;max-height:0px;max-width:0px;opacity:0;overflow:hidden;\">\r\nCrypto adoption grows | Tuesday, October 20, 2026\r\n</div><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"100%\" style=\"background-color: #f6f6f6;text-align: center\"><tr><td style=\"max-width: 600px;\"><!--[if mso]><table style=\"width:600px;\"><tr><td><![endif]--><table style=\"max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; width: 100%;\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr><td height=\"25\" style=\"height: 25px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-left: 35px;\"><a href=\"#\" title=\"AXIOS\"><img src=\"https://static.axios.com/img-email/axios-retina.png\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin-bottom: -1px;\" alt=\"Axios Logo\" width=\"83\" /></a><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cDovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWFtcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe783bf78\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asl5i2.cqo9/2752af9c.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td></tr></table><table style=\"max-width: 600px; width: 100%; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; background: #fff;\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr><td height=\"20\" style=\"height: 20px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"vertical-align: top;\"><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding-right: 3.5%;\" align=\"right\"><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWM2ZDZmNDAwLWNiYWUtMTFmMS04OGIyLWMzYzc2ZDYwZDhhNS5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj10aG91Z2h0LWJ1YmJsZS1hbXBtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa3d9f4d2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color: #222222; font-size: 13px; font-family: 'gordita', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-decoration:underline;\">View in browser</a></td></tr>\r\n</table></td></tr><tr><td height=\"30\" style=\"height: 30px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size: 11px; letter-spacing:1.4px; color: #222222; font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-transform: uppercase;\">Presented By Synchrony</span>\r\n</td></tr><tr><td height=\"16\" style=\"height: 16px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1;\"><span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size: 44px; font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #008dc8; letter-spacing: -1px; line-height: 1;\">Axios AM Thought Bubble</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.5; padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px;\"><span class=\"b\"  style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #222222; font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; \">By\r\nMike Allen\r\n<span style=\"margin: 0 6px;\">&middot;</span>\r\nOct 20, 2026\r\n</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px; padding: 0 3.5%;\">\r\n<p>🎰 <strong>Money 20/20, </strong>a bellwether financial tech event, is underway in Las Vegas, with <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL3Byby9hbGwtZGVhbHM_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWFtcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe61e8fef\" target=\"_blank\">Axios Pro</a> reporters Ryan Lawler and Lucinda Shen inside the hall.</p><ul><li><strong>The buzzy annual gathering</strong> draws industry leaders to explore the latest trends and new technologies powering modern finance. </li><li><strong>In this special edition, </strong>Ryan and Lucinda bring us the latest on a long-promised tech transition that's now being delivered.</li></ul><p><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 397 words ... a 1½-min. read.</em></p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 20px 3.5%; line-height: 1.5;\"><span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size: 27px; font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n1 big thing: Wall Street brings blockchain into the fold\r\n</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td>\r\n<img src=\"https://images.axios.com/E-8VC-xBGYu36KW8OUZHG4xdle0=/1920x1080/smart/2023/12/07/220316-1701986596285.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a pattern of the Wall St. bull and pixelated coins.\">\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.3;\"><span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #848484;\">\r\n<p>Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios</p>\r\n</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"15\" style=\"height: 15px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75; font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<p><strong>LAS VEGAS </strong>— The buzz at Money 20/20 is focused on consumers being on the verge of near-instant banking transfers, including at night or on weekends, <em>Axios' Ryan Lawler and Lucinda Shen report.</em></p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> America's financial giants have talked for years about bringing blockchain — the technology that cryptocurrencies like bitcoin are built on — into their systems. Now they're actually doing it. </p><p><strong>That shift</strong> to instant transfers<strong> </strong>could also make investing faster and more convenient: <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDkvMTcvc2VjLXRva2VuaXphdGlvbi1jcnlwdG8tc3RvY2tzP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj10aG91Z2h0LWJ1YmJsZS1hbXBtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB8e3caac6\" target=\"_blank\">Digital versions of stocks</a> could let investors transfer shares around the clock, even when exchanges are closed. </p><ul><li><strong>\"It's becoming</strong> more mainstream institutionally than it ever has been,\" Digital Currency Group investor Aaron Fu tells Axios, pointing to financial institutions building more blockchain infrastructure in-house.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 How it works:</strong> Financial institutions have begun using private blockchains to instantly track money and investments as they change hands.</p><p><strong>Yes, but:</strong> Using the technology behind cryptocurrencies doesn't necessarily mean using the currencies themselves.</p><ul><li><strong>Banks can create</strong> digital versions of the dollars customers already have on deposit.</li></ul><p><strong>💰 State of play:</strong> Money 20/20 attendees say that the conversation has moved from \"Is this possible?\" (the answer is yes) to figuring out exactly how banks will put these services into the electronic hands of consumers like you and me.</p><ul><li><strong>The </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHRjYy5jb20vcHJlc3MtcmVsZWFzZXMvMjAyNi9kdGNjLXR1cm5zLXRva2VuaXphdGlvbi1pbnRvLXJlYWxpdHk_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWFtcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB31c8aa82\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>industry group</strong></a><strong> </strong>that handles much of the recordkeeping and settlement behind U.S. stock trades is preparing a service that creates digital tokens representing securities held in its system. This is called \"tokenization.\" </li><li><strong>Already,</strong> Citibank has said its tokenized-deposit service operates in seven markets, letting clients move funds between Citi accounts on a private blockchain. </li></ul><p><strong>🔎 Reality check:</strong> Competing tokenization efforts could create different versions of the same asset trading on separate networks. </p><ul><li><strong>That could confuse</strong> investors, reduce liquidity, and make it harder to establish reliable prices.</li></ul><p><strong>The bottom line:</strong> Blockchain is closer than ever to revolutionizing banking. First, banks, brokers and asset managers must connect systems so consumers and investors can move assets between them as easily as within them.</p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"20\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=\"ol-adpad\" style=\"padding: 20px 3.5% 0 3.5%;\"><p class=\"b\"\r\nstyle=\"-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100% !important; margin-bottom: 0 !important; font-size: 11px !important; letter-spacing: 1.4px; color: #008dc8; font-weight:700;\"\r\n>\r\nA MESSAGE FROM SYNCHRONY\r\n</p></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 20px 3.5%; line-height: 1.5;\"><span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size: 26px; color: #222222;  font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;  letter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">AI shopping needs a common language</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td>\r\n<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubGlua2VkaW4uY29tL3B1bHNlL2FpLWNoYW5naW5nLWhvdy1jdXN0b21lcnMtY2hvb3NlLXlvdXItYnJhbmQtcmVhZHktam5oZGU_YXhpb3NfYWRsaW5rPTEmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWFtcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBbbb0be50\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://tpc.googlesyndication.com/pageadimg/imgad?id=CICAgJDV887fcBABGAEoATII5AIpNjV7_18\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" /></a>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"15\" style=\"height: 15px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75;  font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<p><strong>Agents, merchants, issuers and platforms</strong> need a common way to exchange information.</p>\r\n<ul><li>Synchrony is helping shape open standards that can carry product, financing, rewards, permissions and transaction information across AI shopping experiences.</li></ul>\r\n<p>See how Synchrony is <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubGlua2VkaW4uY29tL3B1bHNlL2FpLWNoYW5naW5nLWhvdy1jdXN0b21lcnMtY2hvb3NlLXlvdXItYnJhbmQtcmVhZHktam5oZGU_YXhpb3NfYWRsaW5rPTEmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPXRob3VnaHQtYnViYmxlLWFtcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCbbb0be50\" target=\"_blank\">helping shape AI shopping.</a></p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"l\" style=\"padding:24px 4%;margin:0;line-height:1.75;font-size:16px;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><table width=\"100%\" style=\"margin:0 auto;width:100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size:0\"><img src=https://static.axios.com/img-email/smart-brevity.gif style=\"width:100%;max-width:87px;min-width:64px\" border=\"0\" alt=HQ width=\"87\"/></td><td><table width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;width:100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"padding-left:20px;font-family:'NB International Pro','Helvetica','Helvetica Neue'\" class=\"m\"><div style=\"font-size:17px;color:#333335\" class=\"hq-cta-text-header\">👆 Like this comms style and format?</div><div style=\"padding-top:6px;font-size:14px;color:#656568;line-height:1.5\" class=\"hq-cta-text-body\">It's called Smart Brevity®. <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3NocS5jb20vZGVtbz91dG1fc291cmNlPWF4aW9zLW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249YXhpb3NocS1ubC1mb290ZXImc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB58b1e21c\">Bring it to your org</a> — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact.</div></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr>\r\n</table><!-- End email content --><!-- Start footer -->\r\n<table style=\"max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;width:100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tr><td height=\"20\" style=\"height:20px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:0 5%;line-height:1.75\"><span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.75;color:#333335\"><p>Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.<br><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48016154.594441/aHR0cHM6Ly